window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>This is book 5 in the Spellbound Bookshop paranormal cozy mystery series by </b><b><i>USA TODAY</i></b><b> best-selling Author J.A. Whiting.</b><br> <br> It’s September in the seacoast town of Hamlet, Massachusetts, and Shelby Price is happily running her bookshop and enjoying spending time with friends and her new boyfriend.<br> <br> Last Christmas, Shelby fell off a ladder and hit her head, and when she woke up, she could hear her cat talking to her. Not only could she converse with the feline, but she started to develop some paranormal powers. Initially shocked and frightened by what was going on, Shelby came to accept her new skills and has been working to better understand what she can do with them.<br> <br> The town is preparing for its annual \"Luck of the Sea\" festival, but a string of unlucky accidents threatens to derail the event. Shelby notices a pattern in the accidents that seems related to some pirate legends found in an old book from her shop. With the help of her cat Harper, her friend Lucy, the town detective, and her paranormal skills, can Shelby figure out what’s going on before it is too late?<br> <br> This story has some mild paranormal elements.</p>"; 
